  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> pass through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;intersect the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and be parallel to the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Then the distance of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;from the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p>"
  },
